# Smith calibration ledger — persistence for the release-preflight floor.
#
# The floor (references/eval-gate.md → Calibration anchor) blocks a Kiln version bump when
# routing prose changed since the last recorded calibration without an intervening --validate
# free-ride. It needs a commit to diff against; this file is that commit's home.
#
# Format: exactly one active record line (comments start with #), space-separated:
#   <commit-sha> <coverage> <iso-date> <drift-ratio>
#     commit-sha  — HEAD when the calibration replay ran (what the floor diffs: git diff <sha>..HEAD)
#     coverage    — full-21 | partial-freeride
#     iso-date    — YYYY-MM-DD the calibration ran
#     drift-ratio — reproduced/total vs gold (soft signal, not a gate)
#
# Writers (both overwrite the active record line, never append history):
#   /smith --calibrate     — after a full-21 run: coverage=full-21
#   /smith --validate       — the free-ride records coverage=partial-freeride (only if no full-21
#                             record already covers HEAD's routing prose)
# Reader: the release-preflight floor. A partial-freeride record satisfies the floor only for the
# routing sections its in-scope scenarios covered; a full-21 record satisfies it unconditionally.
